#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - eigen upstream test inventory reporting
# Source package: eigen/3.4.1
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-eigen-3.4.1-upstream-test-statistics-145
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|shadow-ci
phase:                  packaging|testing|ci-gate
error_signature:        PR 声明上游合计 0|少报成立|145/145|EIGEN_DECLARE_TEST

severity:               2
category:               conan|test-reporting|pr-description|review-evidence
match_keywords:         eigen, upstream tests, test/ tree, EIGEN_DECLARE_TEST, underreporting, consumer-only gate, shadow CI
title:                  Eigen upstream test inventory should be written as 145, not 0, when only the consumer gate runs

root_cause:             A header-only package can have a large upstream test tree even when the packaged gate only
                        runs a consumer smoke test. Treating that upstream inventory as zero hides real test scope.
affected_scope:         PR descriptions and reviewer summaries for header-only packages with a separate consumer
                        test_package gate.
verification_cmd:       rg -n "EIGEN_DECLARE_TEST" test

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           separate-upstream-inventory-from-executed-gate
rec_description:        Record the upstream Eigen test inventory using the real test tree count, then state that
                        the shadow gate only executes the consumer test_package. Do not report the upstream count as 0.
rec_command:            python scripts/ohc-run.py prescan --no-writeback --json <extracted eigen-3.4.1 source>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               test-reporting

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      consumer-only-boundary
fallback_description:   If only the consumer package can be validated, document the execution scope separately from
                        the upstream inventory so the reviewer can see the boundary clearly.
fallback_command:       rg -n "EIGEN_DECLARE_TEST" test | Measure-Object
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual

forbid_1_pattern:       上游合计 0.*consumer test_package
forbid_1_reason:        The upstream Eigen test tree exists and should not be collapsed to zero in the PR report.
forbid_1_consequence:   Reviewers treat the PR as underreporting the upstream test surface.

similar_to:             [E035,E307,E309]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-eigen-3.4.1-upstream-test-statistics-145.md
last_updated:           2026-08-28
source_event:           eigen/3.4.1 PR review underreporting fix for upstream test inventory

authors:                codex <codex@noreply.local>
